speechtext:
The House in Committee of Ways and Means, Mr. Boivin in the Chair:
1. Resolved, That lit is expedient to amend The Customs Tariff, 1907, -by inserting the following section immediately after section 8:
8a. Notwithstanding anything in this Act, goods, other than tobacco, cigars, cigarettes, spirituous or alcoholic liquors and articles specified in Schedule A of The West Indies Trade Agreement Act, the produce or manufacture of
British Honduras;
Bermuda;
the Bahamas;
J amaica;
Turks and Caicos Islands ;
the Leeward Islands (Antigua, St. Chr-isto-pher-JNevis, Dominica, Montserrat, and the Virgin Islands) ;
the Windward Islands (Grenada, St. Vincent and St. Lucia) ;
Barbados;
Trinidad and Tobago; and
British Guiana
when (imported direct therefrom shall not be subject at any time to more 'than fifty per centum of the duties imposed on similar goods as set forth in the General Tariff under regulations by the Minister of Customs and Inland - Revenue.
Mr. DuTREMBLAY:	As regards the
duty on tobacco and manufactured cigars, is the duty based on the weight or on the value of the tobacco?
